Learning objectives
After completing this chapter, you will be able to:

distinguish row-oriented text formats from columnar analytical formats;
explain how schema, compression, and column projection affect storage and reads;
design partitions around common filters rather than arbitrary columns;
recognize small-file, over-partitioning, and schema-evolution risks;
